+# Native private text draft, schema 1
+
+This is a new native-authored `TOPIC` draft format on the existing opaque `payloadJson`
+save/restore contract. It is not a conversion of a legacy topic, `ProjectEditDraft`,
+publication bundle, installed W18 component, or receipt. It does not publish or install content.
+
+## Explicit format and editable surface
+
+- Root `schema` is exactly `questify-native-text-draft`; `schemaVersion` is numeric 1.
+- `title` is a string, at most 2,048 UTF-8 bytes and nonblank when saving.
+- `nodes` contains 1–100 objects, each with a unique stable ASCII `id` (1–64 characters,
+  letters/digits/underscore/hyphen), `type: "text"`, and string `text` (at most 65,536 UTF-8 bytes).
+- Only title and existing node text can change in this slice. Node creation/removal/reordering,
+  resource references, media, routes, execution and installed content are not exposed.
+- Total JSON is bounded to 512 KiB and the existing strict parser's 128-level nesting limit.
+
+Unknown root/node/nested properties remain inert and survive save/reopen. The exact-JSON payload
+codec uses the existing strict AST: arbitrary-precision decimal coefficient/exponent numbers,
+byte-distinct Unicode object keys/string values, ordered arrays, booleans and null. It never
+round-trips payload numbers through `Double`, `Decimal`, `NSNumber`, or `JSONSerialization`.
+Lexical JSON spacing/key order/numeric spellings may change; JSON meaning does not. Duplicate
+keys and unsupported structures/versions fail closed. The Codable archive is an opaque JSON
+string; only the explicit `ContentDraftExactJSONPayload` codec produces wire payload JSON.
+Existing Codable payloads continue through the unchanged encoder settings and equality check.
+
+## Actual flow and safety boundary
+
+The normal Account owner-draft destination exposes a new-private-text-draft entry. A validated
+restore of this exact native format exposes its editor entry. All other draft formats retain the
+read-only/unavailable path. Selection carries the real content-draft ID and validated owner/key,
+not a subject ID, W18 owned-component ID or installation receipt.
+
+`NativeTextDraftEntryView` has an optional owner-bound editor factory. Its default is absent:
+the real navigation shows an honest unavailable state and disabled review/save controls. Neither
+AppSession nor production route grants/storage are activated. A future host must supply a fresh
+session/display lease, the reviewed owner-only service grant and the genuine secure durable journal.
+No in-memory or plaintext production fallback exists.
+
+With those injected dependencies, the editor restores or creates its private native draft, edits
+title/text, validates structure, displays the before/after diff, and requires explicit confirmation.
+All mutations use `ContentDraftCoordinator` and its existing immutable journal/prepared-dispatch
+boundary. Dismissal, cancellation or session replacement clears in-memory content and fences late
+results while retaining any uncertain journal command.
+
+A definitive first-attempt 409 preserves local edits. Readback is explicit. Keeping edits applies
+only changed title/text fields to the latest cloud object, preserving newly introduced unknown
+properties and untouched cloud text. Changed node IDs/order block this rebase. The user can choose
+cloud content, or review the rebased diff before any new save. Unknown outcomes allow only the
+exact same-key/body/version retry; reading the cloud record never clears uncertainty.
+
+Installed-module receipt metadata is never read into or written from this payload. There is no
+claim of W18 component editing, licence validation, adaptation rights, publishing, installing,
+new endpoints, or production acceptance. W02/W05 editor prerequisites are advanced only for this
+explicit native subtype; legacy and W18 materialization remain separate work.
+
+## Verification
+
+Authored: 18 focused Swift domain tests, four editor XCUITest scenarios, and two normal-owner
+navigation XCUITest cases. They cover lossless unknown values, schema/owner/size rejection,
+fallback Codable bytes, create/edit/diff/cancel/save/reopen, known-409 rebase, exact uncertain retry,
+late restore/save/401 fencing, account replacement, receipt exclusion and absent grant/journal.
+
+The DEBUG fixture uses the existing sealed in-process recording transport and an explicitly
+synthetic memory journal. It creates no account, HTTP network call or production persistence.
+Offline source-contract assertions, project/resource checks and supplementary Tree-sitter parsing
+are separate evidence. Swift tests, Apple typechecking/builds, simulator interaction, real Keychain/
+APFS durability and live server behavior are NOT_RUN in the Linux authoring workspace. Hosted
+Apple checks for the eventual published revision are required before runtime acceptance.
+
+## Independent prerequisite review
+
+The independent source review tightened three reusable-model boundaries: construction now checks
+aggregate document size immediately; rebase rejects local as well as cloud node identity/order
+changes; and repeated open calls preserve unreviewed local edits and their original diff baseline.
+Three additional Swift behavior tests and two Python source checks cover these cases. Source checks
+passed; the Swift tests remain authored but UNRUN. This acceptance covers the reusable prerequisite
+and recording fixture only. The nil normal-root factory is still unavailable, so normal Account
+editing/saving and durable-system-journal integration are not delivered by this unit.
